society|community-system|NOUN|people living together with shared systems|People considered as a community with shared institutions, customs, and ways of living.|xã hội|Public libraries play an important role in society.|Thư viện công cộng đóng vai trò quan trọng trong xã hội.|Uncountable for social life generally; a society can name a particular community.|0
society|organized-group|NOUN|organization with a shared interest|An organization whose members share a particular interest or purpose.|hội; hiệp hội|The local history society collects photographs of old streets.|Hội lịch sử địa phương sưu tầm ảnh những con phố cũ.|Countable; often part of an organization's name, distinct from society as a whole.|1
weekly|each-week|ADJECTIVE|happening every week|Happening or appearing once each week.|hằng tuần|The village holds a weekly market beside the bridge.|Ngôi làng tổ chức một phiên chợ hằng tuần cạnh cây cầu.|Adjective before a noun or after a linking verb; in this record weekly is not an adverb modifying a verb.|0
celebration|special-event|NOUN|activity marking a happy occasion|An event or activity held to show happiness about a special occasion.|lễ mừng; sự ăn mừng|The staff organized a small celebration for the library's anniversary.|Nhân viên tổ chức một lễ mừng nhỏ nhân dịp kỷ niệm của thư viện.|Countable for an event; uncountable in in celebration of an occasion.|0
fossil|ancient-evidence|NOUN|preserved evidence of ancient life|Preserved remains or traces of a living thing from the distant past.|hóa thạch|The fossil showed the outline of a leaf in the rock.|Hóa thạch cho thấy đường nét của một chiếc lá trong đá.|Countable; may refer to remains or traces, not only bones of animals.|0
into|movement-inside|PREPOSITION|movement to the inside|Used to show movement from outside to the inside of something.|vào; vào trong|She put the folded map into her coat pocket.|Cô ấy bỏ tấm bản đồ đã gấp vào túi áo khoác.|Preposition with a destination inside a place or container; compare in for position without movement.|0
into|change-result|PREPOSITION|result of a change|Used to show the form or state that something has after a change.|thành; trở thành|The volunteers turned the empty shop into a reading room.|Các tình nguyện viên biến cửa hàng trống thành phòng đọc sách.|Used after change verbs such as turn or transform, with the resulting form as its complement.|1
